{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HOS",
  "chapter": 9,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Rejoice not, O Israel, for joy, as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "other",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " people: for thou hast apostatized from thy God, thou hast loved a reward upon every corn-floor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The floor and the wine-press shall not feed them, and the new wine shall fail in her.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They shall not dwell in the LORD'S land; but Ephraim shall return to Egypt, and they shall eat unclean ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Assyria.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They shall not offer wine -",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": " offerings",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the LORD, neither shall they be pleasing to him: their sacrifices ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to them as the bread of mourners; all that eat of it shall be polluted: for their bread for their soul shall not come into the house of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What will ye do in the solemn day, and in the day of the feast of the LORD?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For lo, they are gone because of destruction: Egypt shall gather them up, Memphis shall bury them: the pleasant ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "places",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for their silver, nettles shall possess them: thorns ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in their tabernacles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The days of visitation are come, the days of recompense are come; Israel shall know ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": the prophet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a fool, the spiritual man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mad, for the multitude of thy iniquity, and the great hatred.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The watchman of Ephraim ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with my God: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the prophet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a snare of a fowler in all his ways, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hatred in the house of his God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have deeply corrupted ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "themselves",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", as in the days of Gibeah: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "therefore",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he will remember their iniquity, he will visit their sins.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I found Israel like grapes in the wilderness; I saw your fathers as the first ripe in the fig-tree at her first time: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they went to Baal-peor, and separated themselves to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shame; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " abominations were according as they loved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Ephraim, their glory shall fly away like a bird, from the birth, and from the womb, and from the conception.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though they bring up their children, yet will I bereave them, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that there shall",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "left",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": yes, woe also to them when I depart from them!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ephraim, as I saw Tyre, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " planted in a pleasant place: but Ephraim shall bring forth his children to the murderer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Give them, O LORD: what wilt thou give? give them a miscarrying womb and dry breasts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All their wickedness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Gilgal: for there I hated them: for the wickedness of their doings I will drive them out of my house, I will love them no more: all their princes ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " revolters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ephraim is smitten, their root is dried up, they shall bear no fruit: yes, though they bring forth, yet will I slay ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the beloved ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "fruit",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of their womb.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.9.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.9.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My God will cast them away, because they did not hearken to him: and they shall be wanderers among the nations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
